# Self-hosted runners on this repo

Planning source of truth: `docs/RUNNER_TOPOLOGY.md`.

| Runner            | OS                         | Role        | Use for                                                                 |
| ----------------- | -------------------------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `m4-morphosource` | macOS ARM64                | **Driver**  | MorphoSource, research agent, `make unshelve`, pilot/export as HTTP client to Jetstream, `stage_morphosource_sample.py --phase ct-only` (TIFF stream + crop + gzip NRRD), other "compression and NRRD generation" tasks — **not** local Slicer/nnInteractive, **not** mesh voxelization |
| `DellXPS-wsl-gpu` | Linux x64 (WSL2 + Ubuntu)  | **Light GPU** | Mesh morphometrics, embeddings, `nninteractive_compare` batch jobs, bootstrap smoke, `stage_morphosource_sample.py --phase voxelize-only` (mesh → labelmap on the Mac-built CT grid) — **not** the Jetstream interactive Slicer stack |

## What the Mac mini does and doesn't do

OK on the Mac mini:

- MorphoSource API, manifest/JSONL/CSV parsing
- TIFF/DICOM streaming, crop + stride downsample, gzipped NRRD/NIfTI **writing**
- SHA256, provenance JSON, git ops, GH issue API, `make unshelve`
- HTTP/SSH driver clients to Jetstream / Dell (`slicer_remote_*`, `nninteractive_remote.py`, `eval_project358382_pilot.py`)
- `stage_morphosource_sample.py --phase ct-only`

NOT OK on the Mac mini (route to Dell or Jetstream):

- `vtkPolyDataToImageStencil`, `vtkSelectEnclosedPoints`, `trimesh.contains`, or any per-voxel mesh → labelmap pipeline on a > ~1 M-poly mesh
- nnInteractive / nnU-Net inference, MONAI training, CUDA/MPS inference loops
- Headless or GUI Slicer compute
- `numpy` / `SimpleITK` ops on full-resolution multi-GB volumes
- `stage_morphosource_sample.py --phase voxelize-only` or `--phase all` (the script refuses on `darwin` unless `MORPHOCLAW_FORCE_MAC_VOXELIZE=1`)

If a script you're editing crosses the line (does mesh voxelization or
nnInteractive inference *and* gets called from a Mac runner), split it
into a driver leg + a tool leg, the way `stage_morphosource_sample.py`
splits into `--phase ct-only` + `--phase voxelize-only`.

## Heavy work always goes through `gh workflow run`, never a local Mac terminal

This rule is enforced both by docs (`docs/RUNNER_TOPOLOGY.md`) and by
the scripts themselves: `eval_project358382_pilot.py` and
`nninteractive_compare.py` have Darwin guards that refuse a live run on
macOS, and `morphosource_api_download.download_media()` has a free-disk
pre-check (default 5 GiB; `MORPHOSOURCE_MIN_FREE_GB` to override).

If the user asks you to run the 10-click pilot, the comparison, or any
similar heavy job, the dispatch path is:

```sh
make pilot-dell        # default, works today
make pilot-jetstream   # once the JS2 GHA runner is registered (Phase 3)
make nni-compare-dell  # Phase 2 -- still TODO; use raw gh until then
make tail RUN_ID=<id>  # or: make tail (most recent run)
```

**Never** propose pasting `python .github/scripts/eval_project358382_pilot.py …`
into a Mac terminal as the way to run the pilot. The script will refuse;
that refusal is intentional. The cautionary tale is the 2026-05-24
incident — a local run filled the workspace disk to 100% mid-pilot and
lost two of three specimens. See "2026-05-24 cautionary tale" in
`docs/RUNNER_TOPOLOGY.md`.

The only `python` paths that are still OK in a Mac terminal:

| Path | Why |
| --- | --- |
| `… --help` | argparse only; no compute |
| `… --dry-run` | discovery + validation only |
| `… --replay-from <DIR>` | offline fixture playback; no network, no GPU |
| `… --cached-specimens <FILE> --no-download` | driver orchestration against pre-prepared inputs |
| `… --from-fixture <DIR>` (compare) | PR smoke test path |
| `… --skip-paint-loop` (compare) | alignment-only dry run |
| `make unshelve IP=…` | SSH-only driver work; the one Mac-terminal flow this rule allows for live infra |

Escape hatch (use only after explaining the failure mode to the user):
`--force-local` CLI flag, or `MORPHOCLAW_FORCE_MAC_PILOT=1` env var.

## Routing workflows

Use **the most specific label set**:

```yaml
runs-on: [self-hosted, gpu, nninteractive]   # DellXPS-wsl-gpu (light GPU)
runs-on: [self-hosted, jetstream]            # Jetstream box (when registered)
runs-on: [self-hosted, morphosource]         # Mac mini driver
```

`runs-on: self-hosted` alone is wrong — it can land on the Mac mini for GPU jobs.

Live 10-click / `export_session` from a dev machine: driver on Mac, tool on
Jetstream via `SLICER_WEBSERVER_URL` in `.env` (see `docs/JETSTREAM_UNSHELVE.md`).

## Dell XPS GPU runner operational commands (run from a Cursor terminal on the Dell)

PowerShell wrapper: `scripts/runners/runner-ctl.ps1 <subcommand>`

| Task                  | One-liner                                                                |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Start the runner      | `pwsh scripts/runners/runner-ctl.ps1 start`                              |
| Stop the runner       | `pwsh scripts/runners/runner-ctl.ps1 stop`                               |
| Runner status         | `pwsh scripts/runners/runner-ctl.ps1 status`                             |
| Dispatch a workflow   | `pwsh scripts/runners/runner-ctl.ps1 dispatch runner-smoke.yml -f skip_slicer=true`     |
| List recent runs      | `pwsh scripts/runners/runner-ctl.ps1 runs`                               |
| Tail a run live       | `pwsh scripts/runners/runner-ctl.ps1 tail <run-id>`                      |
| Watch runner log      | `pwsh scripts/runners/runner-ctl.ps1 log`                                |

## Environment overrides

Each runner ships a per-host `.env` next to the runner binary that sets
`ANACONDA_BIN`, `SLICER_BIN`, and `NNINTERACTIVE_HOME`. Workflows must NOT
hardcode macOS paths — they should pull from `${{ env.ANACONDA_BIN }}` etc.
See `scripts/runners/runner-env.example` for the canonical template.

## Adding a new runner

Follow `docs/self-hosted-gpu-runner.md`. Re-using `scripts/runners/setup-wsl-runner.sh`
is idempotent — safe to re-run on an existing box.
